{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["And the reason for <b>\"And Elohim spoke to Noah and to his sons with him\"</b> is through their father, for his sons were not prophets, and Ham had not attained the level of prophecy. And so, \"And YHWH spoke to Ahaz\" (Isaiah 7:10), and so, \"And YHWH spoke to Moses and to Aaron\" (Exodus 7:8), according to the words of our Sages (Sifra, Leviticus 1) — to Moses He said, that he should speak to Aaron. And so He explained at the end of \"And Elohim spoke to Noah\" (Genesis 9:17)."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {0 "Ramban quotes the Sages from Sifra on Leviticus 1; the abbreviation ת\"כ is resolved as Torat Kohanim (Sifra)."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:26:27.410017023Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}